<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Joel of Dotawo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. <a href="/years/1463">1463</a>–<a href="/years/1484">1484</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Joel was a king of Dotawo, the last Christian kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubia">Nubia</a> on the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a>, in the later 15th century. He is known from documents and inscriptions from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gebel-adda">Gebel Adda</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qasr-ibrim">Qasr Ibrim</a>, the latest dated to 1484, which make him the last securely attested king of Christian Nubia.</p></div>
